    "Description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: pfifo_tail_enqueue: Drop new packet when sch-\u003elimit == 0 (CVE-2025-21702)\n\n* kernel: net/sched: ets: Always remove class from active list before deleting in ets_qdisc_change (CVE-2025-71066)\n\n* kernel: HID: wacom: fix out-of-bounds read in wacom_intuos_bt_irq (CVE-2026-43051)\n\n* kernel: net: bridge: use a stable FDB dst snapshot in RCU readers (CVE-2026-46086)\n\n* kernel: Bluetooth: hci_ldisc: Clear HCI_UART_PROTO_INIT on error (CVE-2026-53073)\n\n* kernel: sctp: validate embedded INIT chunk and address list lengths in cookie (CVE-2026-53224)\n\n* kernel: sctp: validate cached peer INIT chunk length in COOKIE_ECHO processing (CVE-2026-53246)\n\n* kernel: ipv4: free inet_opt and ireq_opt after an RCU grace period (CVE-2026-98432)\n\n* kernel: ZDI-CAN-33367: Linux Kernel skbuff skb_zerocopy Improper Ownership Management Local Privilege Escalation Vulnerability ()\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* RHEL9: Fix downstream-only regression from 532af53c [rhel-9.6.z] (JIRA:RHEL-192429)\n\n* RHEL 9: Backport b95e0e792822 [rhel-9.6.z] (JIRA:RHEL-216469)\n\n* Hard lockup experienced with repro from RHEL-282072 [rhel-9.6.z] (JIRA:RHEL-290029)\n\n* The Kernel panic occurred at strlen+0x0 because a race event filter treats the user space pointer as a normal pointer [rhel-9.6.z] (JIRA:RHEL-291140)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
